# Baby Tracker — Data & DB Rules

## Core Types (src/types.ts — source of truth)

```typescript
type EventType = 'NUTRITION' | 'DIAPER' | 'SLEEP' | 'ACTIVITY' | 'WEIGHT' | 'PUMPING' | 'VOMITING';
type ParentType = 'PARENT_A' | 'PARENT_B';

interface BabyEvent {
  id: string;           // 'event_{Date.now()}_{randomStr}'
  timestamp: string;    // ISO 8601 — always UTC
  eventType: EventType;
  loggedBy: ParentType;
  notes?: string;
  deletedAt?: string;   // soft-delete — set by deleteEvent(), filtered by isActiveEvent()
  // payload fields: nutrition?, diaper?, sleep?, activity?, weight?, pumping?, vomiting?
}

interface UserSettings {
  userId: string;       // always 'shared-household' — hardcoded
  parentAName: string;
  parentBName: string;
  defaultBottleType: 'EXPRESSED_MILK' | 'FORMULA';
  customActivities: string[];
}
```

All new types and interfaces go in `src/types.ts`. Never inline in `db.ts` or `App.tsx`.

## Firestore Structure

```
/households/shared-household            ← UserSettings doc
/households/shared-household/events/    ← BabyEvent docs
```

One household. `householdId = 'shared-household'` hardcoded at line ~41. No multi-tenancy.

## Timestamp Convention

- Store: ISO 8601 UTC (`new Date().toISOString()`)
- Display: `Asia/Jerusalem` via `Intl.DateTimeFormat` — helpers are in `server.ts`

## Sleep State Machine

- **Open session:** `sleep.endAt === null` (timer running)
- **Closed session:** `sleep.endAt` is an ISO string, `sleep.durationMinutes` is set
- Only ONE open sleep session at a time. `POST /api/sleep/toggle` enforces this.

## DB Layer Rules

- All Firestore operations: `async/await` + `try/catch`. No exceptions.
- `saveEvent()` uses `set()` with full document — upsert semantics. Use this for create and update.
- `deleteEvent()` uses `update({ deletedAt })` intentionally — stamps only the soft-delete field without overwriting the document. Do not change this to `set()`.
- `isActiveEvent()` filters out soft-deleted events — always use it when returning event lists.
- `getAllEvents()` orders by `timestamp desc`. Has fallback if composite index is missing.
- `getOpenSleepSession()` filters in-memory after fetching SLEEP events — no compound index needed.
- `householdDoc` reference is module-level — not recreated per call.
- Never call Firestore SDK directly from `server.ts` or `src/` — always use exported functions from this file.
